B.IG=s(["The Omni does everything the Radial and the Arc can do \u2014 around a ring, straight across through the pole, or along a curve, any distance. It's your most powerful piece by a wide margin.","Like the Arc, an Omni that stops on the pole and survives a turn there can also come back out on either color next move."],t.s)
B.IH=s(["Every square has a letter and a number. The letter is the ring: A is the pole at the very center, then B, C, D, and E moving outward to the rim.","The number is the wedge \u2014 1 through 24, counting counter-clockwise from the 9 o'clock position. The two pieces on the board mark E7 and B7: same wedge, different rings.","The board wraps all the way around a ring, so a piece circling one never runs out of room. The only real edges are the pole at the center and the rim at the outside."],t.s)
B.II=s(["click","scroll"],t.s)
